-*- mode: org -*-

* 1.6.1 <2026-10-01 Thu>

Bug fix release.  No user-facing command, keybinding, option, hook or
face was added or removed.

** Parsing
+ A brace group or inline math directly followed by a column
  delimiter (e.g. ~{a}& b~ or ~$x$& b~) was merged with the next cell.
+ A last row not terminated by a row delimiter was not counted, so
  moving across the end of the table skipped it or landed in the
  wrong row.  It also wasn't considered when detecting ragged tables.
+ Horizontal-line macros between the last row and ~\end~ (e.g.
  ~\bottomrule~) were parsed as an extra cell, which commands could
  then edit (~insert-column~ produced ~\bottomrule &~).
+ A horizontal-line macro followed by a row starting at the beginning
  of a line was parsed as part of that row's first cell: macro names
  could extend across line breaks.
+ The first cell of every row included the line break before it.  As a
  consequence, swapping rows, killing row or column content and
  deleting columns could join rows onto a single line, and aligning
  left blank lines between rows.
+ Parsing could insert a space after ~\begin{...}~ (and fill an empty
  environment) without marking the buffer as modified and without
  recording the change for undo.
+ Starting the wizard with point on the ~\begin~ line signaled an error.
+ Cells of a previously visited table could be picked up when looking
  for the cell at point.

** Commands
+ ~latex-table-wizard-delete-column~ deleted text outside the current
  row (and even outside the table) when a row had a single cell, e.g.
  in single-column or ragged tables.  The deleted content is now also
  added to the kill ring, as ~latex-table-wizard-delete-row~ does.
+ ~latex-table-wizard-comment-out~ always signaled an error (a local
  variable shadowed the dynamic variable ~comment-end~), and could
  comment out text outside the current row.
+ ~latex-table-wizard-insert-column~, ~latex-table-wizard-delete-column~
  and ~latex-table-wizard-kill-column-content~ failed when called after
  another command that modified the table.
+ ~latex-table-wizard-kill-column-content~ always signaled an error
  after killing the content.
+ ~latex-table-wizard-delete-row~ left a blank line behind.
+ ~latex-table-wizard-edit-cell~ added two spaces to the cell every
  time it was used.  New content longer than the old one is now still
  separated from the delimiters by a space (same for
  ~latex-table-wizard-yank-cell-content~).
+ ~latex-table-wizard-edit-cell~, ~latex-table-wizard-yank-cell-content~
  and ~latex-table-wizard-kill-cell-content~ now run
  ~latex-table-wizard-after-table-modified-hook~ like the other editing
  commands.

** Customization and minor mode
+ Environments added to ~latex-table-wizard-new-environments-alist~
  after the package was loaded were not recognized.
+ The customization interface for ~latex-table-wizard-transient-keys~
  was broken (its ~:type~ was not evaluated).
+ Disabling ~latex-table-wizard-mode~ did not remove its
  ~pre-command-hook~ function, and every activation added a new one.

** Internals
*** New internal functions
  ~+ latex-table-wizard--cell-and-delimiter-bounds COORD~
  ~+ latex-table-wizard--replace-cell-content BEG END STR LEN~
  ~+ latex-table-wizard--cleanup-if-not-in-chain~
  ~+ latex-table-wizard--environments~ (replaces the variable of the same name)

*** Removed internal variables
+ ~latex-table-wizard--environments~ (now a function, see above)

* 1.6.0 <2026-05-03 Sun>

** Complete overhaul of the interals
Every user visible command, keybinding, customization variable, hook,
and face is preserved without change, with backward compatibility.
The rewrite replaces the internal data structures and algorithms with
ones that scale better with table size, resulting in measurable
performance improvements on medium and large tables.  For reference,
we list the functions and variables removed and their replacement
(again, all of them never being part of the public API).

